## Point estimate correlations 

Linear relationships between the median of the posterior distribution of drift rate (TRUE) and drift rate (FALSE) and the three pupil metrics (mean pupil size, peak pupil size and rate of pupil change) can be seen in @fig-corr-point-estimates-supp.



















::: {#fig-corr-point-estimates-supp .cell layout-ncol="1" layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Point estimates correlations between drift rate (TRUE) for Learned and Novel faces and pupil metrics (mean pupil size, peak pupil size and rate of pupil change)](supplementary_files/figure-typst/fig-corr-point-estimates-supp-1.png){#fig-corr-point-estimates-supp-1 fig-align='center'}
:::

::: {.cell-output-display}
![Point estimates correlations between drift rate (FALSE) for Learned and Novel faces and pupil metrics (mean pupil size, peak pupil size and rate of pupil change)](supplementary_files/figure-typst/fig-corr-point-estimates-supp-2.png){#fig-corr-point-estimates-supp-2 fig-align='center'}
:::

Point estimates correlations between drift rate (TRUE) and drift rate (FALSE) and pupil metrics
:::


