## Plausible value correlations

We calculated the plausible value correlations between each posterior draw of drift rate (TRUE) and drift rate (FALSE) and the three pupil metrics (mean pupil size, peak pupil size and rate of pupil change). These distributions can be seen in @fig-plausible-corr-drift-supp and a summary of these distributions can be seen in @tbl-plausible-cor-supp.






::: {#fig-plausible-corr-drift-supp .cell layout-ncol="1" layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Plausible value correlations between drift rate (TRUE) for Learned and Novel faces and pupil metrics (mean pupil size, peak pupil size and rate of pupil change)](supplementary_files/figure-typst/fig-plausible-corr-drift-supp-1.png){#fig-plausible-corr-drift-supp-1 fig-align='center'}
:::

::: {.cell-output-display}
![Plausible value correlations between drift rate (FALSE) for Learned and Novel faces and pupil metrics (mean pupil size, peak pupil size and rate of pupil change)](supplementary_files/figure-typst/fig-plausible-corr-drift-supp-2.png){#fig-plausible-corr-drift-supp-2 fig-align='center'}
:::

Plausible value correlations between drift rate parameters and pupil metrics. Points denote the median of the distribution and error bars represent the 66% and 95% quantile intervals.
